    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4e17941f_eac0c873",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-26T17:11:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does get NAK\u0027d and that means it when it to low power mode, right.\n\nHow would we keep track of the hardware state more closely. We can and should do that.",
      "parentUuid": "7b0869f8_bd684543",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 217,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "55adf5881f64900683bc271391f6c19c62b830c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed9f1a12_9ea8702f",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 218,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-25T22:59:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because the bit PD_LPM_FLAGS_ENGAGED gets cleared after this, coming back to this call, potentially won\u0027t affect this port, but it seems odd schedule this call again at the point where it\u0027s entering low power mode.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 218,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 218,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "55adf5881f64900683bc271391f6c19c62b830c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13159ca7_df6a3767",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 218,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-26T13:54:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we take this route, I would like to clean up this call in to low power mode.  first, it should call into the driver not the tcpci interface directly. Second, I would like it to not touch the PD_LPM_FLAGS_ENGAGED flag\n\nThe one extra call of this hook method just exits quick after doing nothing",
      "parentUuid": "ed9f1a12_9ea8702f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 218,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 218,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "55adf5881f64900683bc271391f6c19c62b830c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17c0c2ab_e937d32c",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-25T22:59:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure the value of maintaining \u0027lpm_engaged\u0027 if it\u0027s cleared independent of when the TCPC access actually takes place. The entry into LPM is much more tightly coupled to the SW state as it happens following the write of I2CIDLE.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 239,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "55adf5881f64900683bc271391f6c19c62b830c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "faa1addd_3838a442",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-26T13:54:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The TCPC access is what calls this method, so this is tracking a hardware bus access causing the exit of low-power mode.",
      "parentUuid": "17c0c2ab_e937d32c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 239,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "55adf5881f64900683bc271391f6c19c62b830c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "436405b5_f7e1c13d",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-26T15:56:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern here is that LPM_ENAGAGED is getting cleared before the TCPC access takes place. So there is some time period when this value doesn\u0027t reflect the state of TCPC itself. But setting this bit happens after the TCPC write, not before.",
      "parentUuid": "faa1addd_3838a442",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 239,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "55adf5881f64900683bc271391f6c19c62b830c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f75b451c_a77b90a4",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-26T17:11:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had it clearing after the tcpc_write at some point, but I couldn\u0027t get the guarantee that I wanted so I put it before just to make the code a little nicer for the sketch out CL.\n\nI agree that putting atomic_clear after the tcpc_write, and and putting the atomic_or before the IDLE command is sent if much better. I just didn\u0027t want to add in the logic to ignore the i2c write for the idle command. But we can and should do that if we go with something like this.",
      "parentUuid": "436405b5_f7e1c13d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 239,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "55adf5881f64900683bc271391f6c19c62b830c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "00bdc5db_07b059ec",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 241,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-25T22:59:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know it\u0027s unlikely, but this mechanism allows for the possibility of one port preventing the other port from going into low power mode if there are periodic accesses since the call is deferred independent of the \u0027port\u0027 variable.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 241,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 241,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "55adf5881f64900683bc271391f6c19c62b830c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e512ed23_19bf79f7",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 241,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-26T13:54:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "True, but if we are accessing a TCPC more frequent than every 10ms indefinitely, we have other power problems to worry about. We could make a separate call per port, but that didn\u0027t seem like it was worth the extra complexity.\n\nIf we go with a variant of this solution, we should definitely comment on that behavior in the code though.",
      "parentUuid": "00bdc5db_07b059ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 241,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 241,
        "endChar": 20
      },
